# Plugins

Chemical supports Scramjet plugins both globally on `<Chemical>` and per frame on `<Frame>` or `<TabFrame>`.

## Global Defaults

Pass `plugins` or `adblock` to `<Chemical>` to apply them to every frame automatically:

```svelte
<script>
  import Chemical from "chemicaljs/Chemical";

  let chemical = $state();
  let ready = $state(false);
</script>

<Chemical adblock={true} bind:ready bind:this={chemical}/>
```

Setting `adblock={false}` on an individual `<Frame>` overrides the global default.

## Adblock Options

The `adblock` prop accepts several formats:

```svelte
<Frame adblock={true} bind:chemical bind:ready/>

<Frame adblock={customRulesString} bind:chemical bind:ready/>

<Frame
  adblock={{
    includeDefault: true,
    extraRulesets: [myCustomRules],
  }}
  bind:chemical
  bind:ready
/>
```

You can also import `AdblockPlugin` directly from `chemicaljs/AdblockPlugin` or pass a factory function receiving `{ chemical, defaultRuleset, AdblockPlugin }`.

## Custom Plugins

Pass a plain plugin object (`{ name, dependencies?, install(frame, plugin) }`), a `ManagedPlugin` instance/class, or a factory function receiving `{ plugins, createPlugin, fetch, createDataURL }`.

```svelte
<script>
  import Chemical from "chemicaljs/Chemical";
  import Frame from "chemicaljs/Frame";

  let chemical = $state();
  let ready = $state(false);

  const logNavPlugin = {
    name: "log-nav",
    install(frame, plugin) {
      plugin.tap(frame.hooks.init.post, (context) => {
        console.log("Loaded:", context.client?.url);
      });
    },
  };
</script>

<Chemical bind:ready bind:this={chemical} plugins={[logNavPlugin]}/>
<Frame bind:chemical bind:ready src="https://example.com"/>
```

You can also create managed plugin instances manually with `chemical.createPlugin({ name, dependencies, install })` after `ready` is `true`.

## Built-in Plugin Exports

Once `ready` is `true`, `chemical.plugins` exposes:

* `ManagedPlugin`
* `HttpCachePlugin`
* `UrlWatcherPlugin`
* `CatchEscapedLinksPlugin`
* `EventHandlerPlugin`
* `LinkHandlerPlugin`
* `AdblockPlugin`
